KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a write to stdout always succeeds: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 2 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Soundness: the stream buffers of provide_standard_stream_objects accept
every character (overflow returns not_eof, xsputn returns the count), so
a write never fails and assertion 1 is reported as holding.  The buffer
has to fail nondeterministically, as the C library model of fwrite can.
